  "title": "Eastern Roman Empire",
  "summary": "After Theodosius I died in January 395 his sons divided the empire, with Arcadius taking the east. The eastern half, later called the Byzantine Empire, lasted until the Ottoman sultan Mehmed II conquered Constantinople on 29 May 1453. Under Justinian I it recovered territory in North Africa, Spain and Italy.",
